Topi Linkala <nes@iki.fi> writes:
> John H. wrote:

> > http://www.gamesetwatch.com/2006/08/_play_what_the_hell_does_q_do_1.php

> One comment. The commands are normally lower case letters. So hjkl and
> yubn is basic movement. Up and down are not shift-period and shift-comma

To be more exact, there are commands for both lowercase and uppercase
letters, they just do different things. HJLKYUNB are also movement keys,
they just normally move further than hjklyunb.
And R is not for reading scrolls as the columnt says, it is for removing
rings and amulets while r is for reading scrolls.
Just like S is for saving, not searching, and s is for saving.

But a bigger _error_ is to say shift-d shows discoveries. It never
does, it is another command to drop stuff. The command to show discoveries
is '\'. I don't know if the original Rogue (or other roguelikes) has it
differently, but this is how it works in Nethack.

The recommendation for sticking with the numpad might work for some
people, but it's not a good advice for laptop users who normally don't
have a separate numpad but have to toggle the normal typewriter keys
between numpad mode and normal mode.

And the Esc key doesn't cancel all commands, only some of them. Mostly it
just skips messages. 

